Check only references visible in the supplied text. Flag a cross-document reference that relies solely on a chapter or section number to locate content. A filename, relative path, or `{Keyword}` can identify the target; Markdown link syntax is not required by this criterion.

Do not mistake numbers in constants, versions, test IDs, GOTCHA IDs, filenames, or headings for references. Do not claim that a path or keyword is invalid unless the supplied context directly proves it; static link and traceability gates check existence.
